  "worked_solution": "This is a rational function, so it is continuous at all points in its domain. To find its domain, we start by factoring the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{3-x}{{x}^{2}-3x} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-x}{x(x-3)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $x\\ne 3.$\n\nThis function is continuous everywhere except at the excluded points $x=0$ and $x=3.$\n\nTherefore, the domain consists of the union of the intervals $(-\\infty ,0),$ $(0,3),$ and $(3,\\infty ),$ namely\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,0)\\cup (0,3)\\cup (3,\\infty )\n$$\n\nand the function is also continuous on this union of intervals.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
